data/

# Allow source-code data files (but keep runtime data/ excluded)
!src/data/
# Same trap, same depth, same reason: `data/` matches a directory named `data` at
# ANY depth, so `src/ui/data/` - the Phase 5 Data Center - would be untracked too.
# The deliverable would pass every gate locally and CI would have no files to
# build. `tests/unit/dataCenter.test.tsx` asserts this negation is present and
# effective, so it cannot regress silently.
!src/ui/data/
# `data/` above is a bare pattern, so it matches a directory named `data` at ANY
# depth - including `tests/data/`, which holds the Phase 5 data-product gate. Without
# this negation the whole gate suite is untracked: `npm run test:data` passes
# locally, and CI simply has no files to run. `tests/data/suiteIntegrity.test.ts`
# asserts this negation is present and effective, so it cannot regress silently.
!tests/data/
public/assets/sprite-manifest.json

# Local opencode tool and plugin config is session-specific, not project files.
# Only the top level is ignored: the specialist definitions in
# .opencode/agents/ are tracked project files and must stay in the repository.
.opencode/*.json
.opencode/*.jsonc
.opencode/*.log
